    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d619">

                <pb facs="0901" n="891" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg891"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/6–245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Secretary of State
                        </hi><anchor n="48" xml:id="d619-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-02">June 2, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>13. It was my understanding that the following telegram had been sent by the
                    President to you directly on May 30:</p>
                <p>“Please inform Soong orally that Marshal Stalin desires to discuss important
                    matters with him in Moscow not later than July first.</p>
                <pb facs="0902" n="892" xml:id="pg892"/>
                <p>“We will provide air transportation to Moscow upon receipt of advance information
                    of the date of his departure.</p>
                <p>“For your information this proposed meeting is for a discussion of the tripartite
                    agreement reached at Yalta in regard to Japan.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d619-f1" n="48" type="source" xml:id="d619-f1-content">
                <p>Secretary of State Stettinius was attending the United Nations Conference at San
                    Francisco.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
